Release 1.5 (August 2026)
-------------------------
* Add encrypted protocol v4 with Noise XXpsk3, Argon2id, X25519,
  ChaCha20-Poly1305, receiver indexes, and replay protection
* Bind sticky peer identity to the authenticated Noise public key
* Add server-key pinning, optional downgrade refusal, and identity inspection
* Add RFC 1929 SOCKS5 authentication with a private password file
* Add JSON peer listing and portable ICMP/entropy diagnostics
* Add complete v4 framing, tamper, wrong-PSK, replay, and package tests
* Add IPv6 server-name/literal resolution and ICMPv6 as an outer carrier;
  the virtual VPN network remains IPv4
* Switch authenticated peer traffic inside the server without host iptables,
  and use LocalAppData for native Windows state
* Restore encrypted data-plane performance with in-place AEAD, contiguous ACK
  tracking, optimized release builds, and single-threaded opportunistic Linux
  packet batching
* Raise the userspace TCP send and receive windows for high-bandwidth,
  higher-latency VPN paths to 6 MiB and 8 MiB respectively instead of capping
  throughput at one small window per round trip
* Use conventional sequential ICMP echo tokens for current sessions, add
  per-peer gap/late/duplicate telemetry, and briefly reorder only inner data
  after a late packet proves the path reorders; loss-only and normal paths
  remain zero-copy and do not incur reorder delay

Release 1.4 (July 2026)
-----------------------
* Add an optional adapter-free userspace client using statically embedded lwIP
* Add SOCKS5 TCP CONNECT and UDP ASSOCIATE access to every VPN peer
* Add inbound VPN port sharing with loopback-by-default and explicit target maps
* Add opt-in all-TCP-port sharing with explicit mappings taking precedence
* Add unprivileged ping-socket support on POSIX systems and Windows IP Helper transport
* Add isolated-package userspace integration tests without TUN or build dependencies

Release 1.3 (July 2026)
-----------------------
* Add protocol v3 with session-scoped sequence numbers and rolling ACKs
* Replace the default fixed poll window with adaptive request credits
* Probe and use direct echo replies, with automatic fallback and re-upgrade
* Add transport unit tests and privileged failure/recovery CI coverage

Release 1.2 (July 2026)
-----------------------
* Add persistent random client device identities
* Add server-side sticky leases with least-recently-seen offline eviction
* Add peer listing, device-id inspection, and protocol fallback for old servers

Release 1.1 (November 2022)
---------------------------
* Switch to utun devices on macOS (thanks to unkernet)

Release 1.0 (November 2016)
---------------------------
* Added cygwin support
* Remove supplementary groups when dropping privileges
* Fixed compile error on FreeBSD

Release 0.4.4 (February 2014)
-----------------------------
* Fixed writing beyond array bounds
* Fixed some smaller bugs
* Clean exit on signal
* Improved error reporting

Release 0.4.3 (Mai 2013)
------------------------
* Fixed tunemu compiling issue

Release 0.4.2 (Mai 2013)
